#N canvas 20 20 702 718 10;
#N canvas 60 60 620 520 readme 0;
#X text 10 10 tx81zn~ FM editor \; \; [txfm <bus>] sends to [s <bus>] (the [r <bus>] in front of tx81zn~) and reads outlet 2 of tx81zn~ from [r <bus>-out]. In your own patch: [r tx1] -> [tx81zn~ <rom> <nvram>] -> outlet 2 -> [s tx1-out] and [txfm tx1]. [txedit tx1] on the same bus shows every single parameter. \; \; The algorithm gives the operators roles: C = the carriers (what you hear) \, A = the modulator of the main carrier OP1 \, B = the other modulators. A control of a role changes all of its operators and shows the value of the first one. Roles of the 8 algorithms (manual numbering \, > = modulates): 1-4 C:1 A:2 B:3+4 \, 5 C:1+3 A:2 B:4 \, 6 and 7 C:1+2+3 A:4 \, 8 C:1+2+3+4. A control without an operator in its role shows - and does nothing. \; \; SYN 1: algorithm \, ratio of C / A / B (frequency ratio \, fine on SYN 2) \, mod A / B = output level of the modulators (brightness) \, feedback of OP4 \, mix = carriers against each other (only with several carriers: left the main carrier OP1 \, right the others). \; \; SYN 2: waveform W1-W8 per role \, detune (spreads all operators around the centre) \, fine ratio per role \, level C = output level of the carriers. \; \; ENV C / A / B: envelope of the role (C = the amplitude \, A and B = the brightness): attack \, decay \, sustain level \, fade (decay 2 while the key is held) \, release \, velocity sensitivity \, level and rate scaling along the keyboard. \; \; LFO: speed \, wave \, delay \, pitch and amp depth \, pitch and amp sensitivity \, key sync. VOICE: poly / mono \, bend range \, portamento mode and time \, transpose \, LFO amp modulation on / off per role. \; \; Changing the algorithm keeps the operator settings: an operator that becomes a carrier sounds with its output level (level C / mix)., f 92;
